# Chart UI entrypoints (do not waste edits on the wrong `index.html`)

## Canonical live app (what `/chart/index.html` serves in production)

1. **FastAPI** prefers `chart/dist-v9/index.html` when `chart/dist-v9/` exists (`chart/api_server.py`).
2. **Sources**: `chart v 1.4/talaria-design/` — especially `live/index.html`, `live/main.jsx`, `src/TalariaV8bLive.jsx`.
3. **Build**: from `talaria-design/`, run `npm run build:live` → output goes to `chart/dist-v9/`.
4. **Shared engine**: `chart/chart.js`, `chart/modules/*.js` — loaded by URLs under `/chart/` (not bundled inside the React chunk).

## Legacy files (avoid editing unless you intentionally need the old workflow)

- **`chart/legacy-index.html`** — former monolithic page (all deferred scripts). Served at **`/chart/legacy-index.html`**. Use only for fallback / comparison.
- **`chart/index.html`** — short **stub** that explains the above (not the full app).
- **`chart/index.v9.html`** — another large legacy export; same mental model as `legacy-index.html`.

When fixing chart behavior for the deployed site, **edit V9 sources + `chart.js` / modules**, rebuild **`dist-v9`**, bump **`?v=`** on script tags if needed, and deploy **`chart/dist-v9/`** plus updated **`chart/chart.js`** (and any touched **`chart/modules/`** files).
